<title>USA: Franklin Elec completes $60mln financing.</title>
<headline>Franklin Elec completes $60mln financing.</headline>
<dateline>BURLINGTON, N.J. 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franklin Electronic Publishers Inc said on Monday it had completed a $60 million financing arrangement by issuing $40 million in Senior Notes due 2007 to several insurance companies and by executing a new $20 million credit agreement with Chase Manhattan Bank and Summit Bank.</p>
<p>The credit agreement provides for a new unsecured revolving line of credit that replaces Franklin's secured lending arrangement that was in place with Chemical Bank prior to the Chase Manhattan merger, the company said.</p>
<p>The senior notes bear a coupon interest rate of 7.71 percent. Interest under the credit agreement is set at the prime rate or one percent over LIBOR (London Interbank Offered Rate).</p>
</text>
